Hi,

I've just acquired a DS20 with 2 cpus and a couple of dac960 
controllers. Done a debian base install from the latest netinst release 
candidate, all worked fine (except it didn't find the cd drive on the 
sym53c8xx controller until I loaded the module manually). Then I 
installed the 2.6.8 smp kernel kernel (2.6.8-1-smp off the cd, but also 
see exactly the same problem with the latetest  2.6.8-2-smp  package, 
2.6.8-7). It hangs striaght after printing the banner:

DAC960: ***** DAC960 RAID Driver Version 2.5.47 of 14 November 2002 *****
DAC960: Copyright 1998-2001 by Leonard N. Zubkoff <lnz@dandelion.com>

The 2.6.9-2-generic (uniprocessor) works  fine:

DAC960: ***** DAC960 RAID Driver Version 2.5.47 of 14 November 2002 *****
DAC960: Copyright 1998-2001 by Leonard N. Zubkoff <lnz@dandelion.com>
DAC960#0: Configuring Mylex DAC960PU PCI RAID Controller
DAC960#0:   Firmware Version: 2.70-0-03, Channels: 3, Memory Size: 8MB
DAC960#0:   PCI Bus: 0, Device: 9, Function: 0, I/O Address: 0x8080
DAC960#0:   PCI Address: 0xA08A000 mapped at 0xFFFFFD000A08A000, IRQ 
Channel: 23
DAC960#0:   Controller Queue Depth: 64, Maximum Blocks per Command: 1024
DAC960#0:   Driver Queue Depth: 63, Scatter/Gather Limit: 17 of 17 Segments
DAC960#0:   Stripe Size: 64KB, Segment Size: 64KB, BIOS Geometry: 128/32
DAC960#0:   Physical Devices:
DAC960#0:     0:0  Vendor: DEC       Model: RZ1DF-CB (C) DEC  Revision: 0372

[....]

and the machine comes up fine.

Anyone seen this before? Anyone have an SMP  box with a dac960 working 
with the
latest kernels?

Cheers,

	David




