Sigh. Since 2.6.8, SMP and the dac960 driver doesn't play nice, I 
decided to try building the 2.6.10 source from unstable. That actually 
gets me up and running (woo!), but it has some nasty issues... as can be 
seen from the subject!

The odd thing is that _there is no section 27_ in my scsi module; its 
only got 24 sections.

This is with kernel-source-2.6.10 v 2.6.10-5, gcc version 3.3.5 (Debian 
1:3.3.5-8), binutils 2.15-5.

I noticed while compiling that I get:

{standard input}: Assembler messages:
{standard input}:5: Warning: setting incorrect section attributes for .got

once for each .o file. Don't know if its relevant...

Am I missing something really obvious??

Cheers,

